        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;strokeColor=#d6b656;fillColor=#fff2cc;spacing=8;strokeWidth=2;" value="&lt;b&gt;Changa ERD (Cloud Firestore)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;PK primary key&lt;div&gt;FK foreign key&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;? optional field&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;Crow&#39;s foot = many&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;bar = one&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;circle = optional&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each table is a collection; its Firestore path is under the name.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;id / uid / pin&lt;/b&gt; are document IDs, and &lt;b&gt;householdId&lt;/b&gt; on sub-collections comes from the path: keys, not stored fields.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Deliberate duplicates:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;households.pin = householdPins ID (lookup without reading households)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;debts.creditorUid = expenses.paidByUid (Firestore has no joins)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;users.householdId = the household where the user has a members document (saves a collection-group query at login; the app re-checks it is still valid).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
